From 0e19e45479a5dfb8eedc3d6fd5e81909186c6ba9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 10:14:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Read SAGA grids by default, add the use_gdal option to
 VRaster and LandslideMask

VRaster and LandslideMask read SAGA grids without GDAL by default.
With use_gdal=True, GDAL reads the raster (any GDAL-compatible format).

- utils.read_raster(rasterfn, use_gdal=False) chooses the reader.
- raster2array and get_nodata_value use GDAL only again: they raise an
  ImportError without GDAL instead of silently using the SAGA reader.
- VRaster and LandslideMask have no writers, array2raster and
  array2raster_saga stay in utils.
- Add tests for the option. Add the test for a categorical layer with
  nodata cells inside the study area (both modes).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015d85GY593taEw5VGPtHE4q
